/-!
# Noetherian descent of the fibres of a finite type algebra

Let `A → B` be a ring map of finite type and let `L` be a Noetherian `A`-algebra — in practice a
residue field `κ(𝔭)` of `A`. The fibre `B ⊗_A L` is already the base change of a finite type
algebra over a subring of `A` of finite type over `ℤ`, and one such subring serves two prescribed
fibres simultaneously.

Write `B = A[X_1, …, X_n]/I`. For a subalgebra `A₀ ⊆ A` of finite type over `ℤ` put
`I₀ = I ∩ A₀[X]`, so that `A₀[X]/I₀` is the `A₀`-subalgebra of `B` generated by the images of the
variables. Since `L[X]` is Noetherian, the ideal `I · L[X]` is generated by the images of finitely
many elements of `I`; as soon as `A₀` contains all of their coefficients we get
`I₀ · L[X] = I · L[X]`, and hence `B ⊗_A L = (A₀[X]/I₀) ⊗_{A₀} L`. Taking `A₀` large enough to
work for two fibres at once, and to contain the coefficients of a prescribed finite set of
polynomials, is `MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq`.

## Main results

* `Algebra.isPushout_quotient`: base change of a quotient is the quotient by the extended ideal,
  as a pushout square.
* `Algebra.isPushout_quotient_mvPolynomial`: base change of a presented algebra,
  `(A[X]/I) ⊗_A L = L[X]/I · L[X]`, as a pushout square.
* `Ideal.exists_finite_subset_span_image_eq_map`: the extension of an ideal along a ring map to a
  Noetherian ring is generated by the images of finitely many elements of the ideal.
* `MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_mem_range_map`: a finite set of polynomials over `A` has all
  its coefficients in a subalgebra of `A` of finite type over `ℤ`.
* `MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq`: **the descent.** For two Noetherian
  `A`-algebras `L₁`, `L₂` there is a subalgebra `A₀ ⊆ A` of finite type over `ℤ`, containing a
  prescribed one and the coefficients of a prescribed finite set of polynomials, with
  `(I ∩ A₀[X]) · Lᵢ[X] = I · Lᵢ[X]` for `i = 1, 2`.
* `MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv`, `MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_tensorQuotientComap_eq`:
  under that identity the two fibres are isomorphic, and in particular have the same Krull
  dimension.
* `IsUnit.of_faithfullyFlat`, `not_isUnit_of_faithfullyFlat`,
  `Ideal.notMem_minimalPrimes_of_faithfullyFlat`: the three conditions on an element that descend
  along a faithfully flat algebra map.
* `Module.FaithfullyFlat.of_isPushout`, `Algebra.FiniteType.of_isPushout`: faithful flatness and
  finite type ascend along a base change.
* `Ideal.residueFieldAlgebra`, `Ideal.isScalarTower_residueField`,
  `Ideal.residueFieldMap_injective`: the residue field extension `κ(𝔭) → κ(𝔭')` along a ring map,
  as an algebra structure that is not a global instance.

## Implementation notes

`MvPolynomial.algebraMvPolynomial`, the `A[X]`-algebra structure on `L[X]` induced by an
`A`-algebra structure on `L`, is only a local instance in Mathlib. The pushout statements about
polynomial rings use it and `isScalarTower_quotient_mvPolynomial` as local instances, while
`MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq` is stated with explicit `MvPolynomial.map` ring
homomorphisms, since its subalgebra `A₀` is produced existentially.

For a subalgebra `A₀ : Subalgebra ℤ A`, the instances `Algebra A₀ L` and `IsScalarTower A₀ A L`
are `Subalgebra.toAlgebra` and `IsScalarTower.subalgebra`. A `letI` defining `Algebra A₀ L` as the
composite `A₀ → A → L` does not work with `IsScalarTower`, whose `SMul A₀ L` argument still
resolves to `Subalgebra.instSMulSubtypeMem`.

Rewriting the ideal inside an `Algebra.IsPushout` statement is not type correct, since the
`Algebra` instance on the quotient depends on the ring homomorphism being rewritten; the fibres
are compared through `Ideal.map_algebraMap_mvPolynomial_comap_eq` and
`Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq` instead.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 053R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/053R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00R1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00R1)
-/

@[expose] public section

open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra
attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.algebraMvPolynomial

/-!
### Base change of a quotient
-/

/-- **Base change of a quotient.** For an `R`-algebra `S` and an ideal `J` of `R`, the square
`R → R ⧸ J`, `S → S ⧸ J · S` is a pushout square: `(R ⧸ J) ⊗[R] S = S ⧸ J · S`. -/
public theorem Algebra.isPushout_quotient (R S : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
    (J : Ideal R) :
    Algebra.IsPushout R (R ⧸ J) S (S ⧸ J.map (algebraMap R S)) :=
  Algebra.IsPushout.of_equiv (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor S J).symm
    (by
      ext s
      refine (Algebra.TensorProduct.quotIdealMapEquivQuotTensor S J).symm_apply_eq.mpr ?_
      simp [Algebra.TensorProduct.right_algebraMap_apply])

/-- The scalar tower `A → A[X] ⧸ I → L[X] ⧸ I · L[X]`. -/
public theorem isScalarTower_quotient_mvPolynomial (A L : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra A L] {σ : Type*} (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ A)) :
    IsScalarTower A (MvPolynomial σ A ⧸ I)
      (MvPolynomial σ L ⧸ I.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ L))) :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x => by
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ A ⧸ I),
      Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_quotient_map_quotient,
      IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A (MvPolynomial σ L)
        (MvPolynomial σ L ⧸ I.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ L))),
      Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
    congr 1
    simp [← MvPolynomial.algebraMap_eq, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A L (MvPolynomial σ L)]

attribute [local instance] isScalarTower_quotient_mvPolynomial

/-- **Base change of a presented algebra.** For an `A`-algebra `L` and an ideal `I` of a
polynomial ring over `A`, the fibre of `A[X] ⧸ I` over `L` is `L[X] ⧸ I · L[X]`:
`(A[X] ⧸ I) ⊗[A] L = L[X] ⧸ I · L[X]`. -/
public theorem Algebra.isPushout_quotient_mvPolynomial (A L : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra A L] {σ : Type*} (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ A)) :
    Algebra.IsPushout A L (MvPolynomial σ A ⧸ I)
      (MvPolynomial σ L ⧸ I.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ L))) :=
  ((Algebra.IsPushout.comp_iff A (MvPolynomial σ A) L (MvPolynomial σ L)
    (T := MvPolynomial σ A ⧸ I)
    (T' := MvPolynomial σ L ⧸ I.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ L)))).mpr
    (Algebra.isPushout_quotient (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ L) I)).symm

/-- Quotients by equal ideals have the same Krull dimension. -/
public theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_congr {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {J₁ J₂ : Ideal R}
    (h : J₁ = J₂) : ringKrullDim (R ⧸ J₁) = ringKrullDim (R ⧸ J₂) := by
  subst h; rfl

/-!
### The descent of a presentation to a subalgebra of finite type over `ℤ`
-/

/-- If a subset `s` of an ideal `I` of `R` has `v '' s` generating `I · S`, and every element of
`s` comes from `R₀` along `u : R₀ →+* R`, then the contraction of `I` to `R₀` already generates
`I · S`. -/
public theorem Ideal.map_comap_comp_eq_map_of_span_image
    {R₀ R S : Type*} [CommRing R₀] [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (u : R₀ →+* R) (v : R →+* S) (I : Ideal R) (s : Set R)
    (hs : s ⊆ (I : Set R)) (hspan : I.map v = Ideal.span (v '' s))
    (hrange : ∀ f ∈ s, f ∈ Set.range u) :
    (I.comap u).map (v.comp u) = I.map v := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    exact fun x hx => Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem v hx)
  · rw [hspan, Ideal.span_le]
    rintro y ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨f₀, rfl⟩ := hrange f hf
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ (Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (hs hf))

/-- The extension of an ideal along a ring map to a Noetherian ring is generated by the images of
finitely many elements of the ideal. -/
public theorem Ideal.exists_finite_subset_span_image_eq_map {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (f : R →+* S) [IsNoetherianRing S] (I : Ideal R) :
    ∃ s ⊆ (I : Set R), s.Finite ∧ I.map f = Ideal.span (f '' s) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ : (I.map f).FG := IsNoetherian.noetherian _
  have hmap : I.map f = Ideal.span (f '' (I : Set R)) := by
    rw [← Ideal.map_span, Ideal.span_eq]
  have hmem : ∀ y : S, ∃ T : Finset S, ↑T ⊆ f '' (I : Set R) ∧
      (y ∈ t → y ∈ Ideal.span (T : Set S)) := by
    intro y
    by_cases hy : y ∈ t
    · exact (Submodule.mem_span_finite_of_mem_span
        (show y ∈ Ideal.span (f '' (I : Set R)) from
          hmap ▸ ht ▸ Ideal.subset_span (by exact_mod_cast hy))).imp
        fun _ h => ⟨h.1, fun _ => h.2⟩
    · exact ⟨∅, by simp, fun h => absurd h hy⟩
  choose T hT1 hT2 using hmem
  have hsub : (↑(t.biUnion T) : Set S) ⊆ f '' (I : Set R) := fun x hx => by
    obtain ⟨y, -, hy⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.mp (by exact_mod_cast hx); exact hT1 y hy
  have heq : I.map f = Ideal.span (↑(t.biUnion T) : Set S) := by
    refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
    · rw [← ht, Ideal.span_le]
      exact fun y hy => Ideal.span_mono
        (fun x hx => by exact_mod_cast Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨y, by exact_mod_cast hy,
          by exact_mod_cast hx⟩) (hT2 y (by exact_mod_cast hy))
    · rw [hmap, Ideal.span_le]
      exact fun x hx => Ideal.subset_span (hsub hx)
  exact (Set.exists_subset_image_finite_and (f := (f : R → S)) (s := (I : Set R))
      (p := fun u => I.map f = Ideal.span u)).mp
    ⟨(↑(t.biUnion T) : Set S), hsub, (t.biUnion T).finite_toSet, heq⟩

/-- A finite set of polynomials over `A` has all its coefficients in a subalgebra of `A` of finite
type over `ℤ`, which may be taken to contain any prescribed such subalgebra. -/
public theorem MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_mem_range_map {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    {σ : Type*} (s : Set (MvPolynomial σ A)) (hs : s.Finite) (A₁ : Subalgebra ℤ A)
    (hA₁ : A₁.FG) :
    ∃ A₀ : Subalgebra ℤ A, A₁ ≤ A₀ ∧ A₀.FG ∧
      ∀ f ∈ s, f ∈ Set.range (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)) := by
  classical
  refine ⟨A₁ ⊔ Algebra.adjoin ℤ ↑(hs.toFinset.biUnion MvPolynomial.coeffs), le_sup_left,
    hA₁.sup (Subalgebra.fg_adjoin_finset _), fun f hf => ?_⟩
  rw [MvPolynomial.mem_range_map_iff_coeffs_subset]
  intro c hc
  refine ⟨⟨c, (le_sup_right : Algebra.adjoin ℤ _ ≤ _) (Algebra.subset_adjoin ?_)⟩, rfl⟩
  exact_mod_cast Finset.mem_biUnion.mpr ⟨f, hs.mem_toFinset.mpr hf, by exact_mod_cast hc⟩

/-- **Noetherian descent of a presentation.** Let `I` be an ideal of a polynomial ring over `A` in
finitely many variables and let `L₁`, `L₂` be Noetherian `A`-algebras. Then any subalgebra of `A`
of finite type over `ℤ` is contained in one, `A₀`, still of finite type over `ℤ`, which contains
the coefficients of a prescribed finite set `G` of polynomials and for which the contraction
`I ∩ A₀[X]` already generates `I · Lᵢ[X]` for `i = 1, 2`. -/
public theorem MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {σ : Type*} [Finite σ] (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ A))
    (L₁ L₂ : Type*) [CommRing L₁] [CommRing L₂] [Algebra A L₁] [Algebra A L₂]
    [IsNoetherianRing L₁] [IsNoetherianRing L₂]
    (G : Set (MvPolynomial σ A)) (hG : G.Finite) (A₁ : Subalgebra ℤ A) (hA₁ : A₁.FG) :
    ∃ A₀ : Subalgebra ℤ A, A₁ ≤ A₀ ∧ A₀.FG ∧
      (∀ f ∈ G, f ∈ Set.range (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))) ∧
      (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
          ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L₁)).comp (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
        = I.map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L₁)) ∧
      (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
          ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L₂)).comp (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
        = I.map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L₂)) := by
  obtain ⟨s₁, hs₁I, hs₁fin, hs₁⟩ :=
    Ideal.exists_finite_subset_span_image_eq_map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L₁)) I
  obtain ⟨s₂, hs₂I, hs₂fin, hs₂⟩ :=
    Ideal.exists_finite_subset_span_image_eq_map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L₂)) I
  obtain ⟨A₀, hA₁A₀, hA₀fg, hrange⟩ :=
    MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_mem_range_map (G ∪ s₁ ∪ s₂)
      ((hG.union hs₁fin).union hs₂fin) A₁ hA₁
  exact ⟨A₀, hA₁A₀, hA₀fg, fun f hf => hrange f (by simp [hf]),
    Ideal.map_comap_comp_eq_map_of_span_image _ _ I s₁ hs₁I hs₁
      (fun f hf => hrange f (by simp [hf])),
    Ideal.map_comap_comp_eq_map_of_span_image _ _ I s₂ hs₂I hs₂
      (fun f hf => hrange f (by simp [hf]))⟩

/-- The descent identity of `MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq`, restated with the
`A₀[X]`-algebra structure on `L[X]` rather than with explicit `MvPolynomial.map`s. -/
public theorem Ideal.map_algebraMap_mvPolynomial_comap_eq
    {A₀ A L : Type*} [CommRing A₀] [CommRing A] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra A₀ A] [Algebra A L] [Algebra A₀ L] [IsScalarTower A₀ A L]
    {σ : Type*} (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ A))
    (h : (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
        ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)).comp (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
      = I.map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L))) :
    (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A₀) (MvPolynomial σ L))
      = I.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ L)) := by
  have hl : algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A₀) (MvPolynomial σ L)
      = (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)).comp (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)) := by
    ext f
    · simp [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A₀ A L]
    · simp
  have hr : algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ L)
      = MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L) := by
    ext f <;> simp
  rwa [hl, hr]

/-!
### Comparison of the fibres
-/

/-- **The two fibres agree.** Under the descent identity of
`MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq`, the fibre of `A₀[X] ⧸ I ∩ A₀[X]` over `L` is the
fibre of `A[X] ⧸ I` over `L`. -/
public noncomputable def MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv
    {A₀ A L : Type*} [CommRing A₀] [CommRing A] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra A₀ A] [Algebra A L] [Algebra A₀ L] [IsScalarTower A₀ A L]
    {σ : Type*} (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ A))
    (h : (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
        ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)).comp (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
      = I.map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L))) :
    L ⊗[A₀] (MvPolynomial σ A₀ ⧸ I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
      ≃ₐ[L] L ⊗[A] (MvPolynomial σ A ⧸ I) :=
  have h' := Ideal.map_algebraMap_mvPolynomial_comap_eq (A₀ := A₀) (L := L) I h
  haveI := Algebra.isPushout_quotient_mvPolynomial A₀ L
    (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
  haveI := Algebra.isPushout_quotient_mvPolynomial A L I
  (Algebra.IsPushout.equiv A₀ L
      (MvPolynomial σ A₀ ⧸ I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
      (MvPolynomial σ L ⧸ (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A₀) (MvPolynomial σ L)))).trans
    ((Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq L h').trans
      (Algebra.IsPushout.equiv A L (MvPolynomial σ A ⧸ I)
        (MvPolynomial σ L ⧸ I.map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ L)))).symm)

/-- The two fibres of `MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv` have the same Krull dimension. -/
public theorem MvPolynomial.ringKrullDim_tensorQuotientComap_eq
    {A₀ A L : Type*} [CommRing A₀] [CommRing A] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra A₀ A] [Algebra A L] [Algebra A₀ L] [IsScalarTower A₀ A L]
    {σ : Type*} (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ A))
    (h : (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
        ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)).comp (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
      = I.map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L))) :
    ringKrullDim (L ⊗[A₀] (MvPolynomial σ A₀ ⧸ I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))))
      = ringKrullDim (L ⊗[A] (MvPolynomial σ A ⧸ I)) :=
  ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv I h).toRingEquiv

/-- `MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv` on a tensor of a scalar with the class of a
polynomial over `A₀`: it pushes the polynomial forward to `A` and leaves the scalar alone. -/
public theorem MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv_tmul_mk
    {A₀ A L : Type*} [CommRing A₀] [CommRing A] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra A₀ A] [Algebra A L] [Algebra A₀ L] [IsScalarTower A₀ A L]
    {σ : Type*} (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ A))
    (h : (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
        ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)).comp (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
      = I.map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)))
    (c : L) (f : MvPolynomial σ A₀) :
    MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv I h (c ⊗ₜ[A₀] Ideal.Quotient.mk _ f) =
      c ⊗ₜ[A] Ideal.Quotient.mk I (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A) f) := by
  have := Algebra.isPushout_quotient_mvPolynomial A L I
  have := Algebra.isPushout_quotient_mvPolynomial A₀ L
    (I.comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
  apply (Algebra.IsPushout.equiv A L (MvPolynomial σ A ⧸ I)
    (MvPolynomial σ L ⧸ I.map
      (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ A) (MvPolynomial σ L)))).injective
  simp only [MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv, AlgEquiv.trans_apply,
    AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply, Algebra.IsPushout.equiv_tmul]
  rw [map_mul, AlgEquiv.commutes]
  congr 1
  change (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq L _)
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ L) f)) =
    Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)
      (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A) f))
  rw [Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq_mk, MvPolynomial.map_map,
    ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A₀ A L]

/-- The kernel of the restriction of a presentation `A[X] ↠ T` to `A₀[X]` is the contraction of
the kernel of the presentation. -/
public theorem MvPolynomial.ker_restriction_eq_comap_ker
    {A₀ A T : Type*} [CommRing A₀] [CommRing A] [CommRing T]
    [Algebra A₀ A] [Algebra A T] [Algebra A₀ T] [IsScalarTower A₀ A T]
    {σ : Type*} (presentation : MvPolynomial σ A →ₐ[A] T)
    (restriction : MvPolynomial σ A₀ →ₐ[A₀] T)
    (hrestriction : ∀ f, restriction f = presentation (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A) f)) :
    RingHom.ker restriction =
      (RingHom.ker presentation).comap (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)) := by
  ext f
  simp only [RingHom.mem_ker, Ideal.mem_comap, hrestriction]

/-- **The two fibres agree, in terms of the descended subalgebra.** Let `A[X] ↠ T` be a
presentation and let `A₀ ⊆ A` be a subalgebra for which the descent identity of
`MvPolynomial.exists_fg_subalgebra_map_comap_eq` holds at `L`. Then the fibre over `L` of the
`A₀`-subalgebra of `T` generated by the images of the variables is the fibre over `L` of `T`. -/
public noncomputable def MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv
    {A₀ A T L : Type*} [CommRing A₀] [CommRing A] [CommRing T] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra A₀ A] [Algebra A T] [Algebra A₀ T] [IsScalarTower A₀ A T]
    [Algebra A L] [Algebra A₀ L] [IsScalarTower A₀ A L]
    {σ : Type*} (presentation : MvPolynomial σ A →ₐ[A] T)
    (hsurjective : Function.Surjective presentation)
    (restriction : MvPolynomial σ A₀ →ₐ[A₀] T)
    (hrestriction : ∀ f, restriction f = presentation (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A) f))
    (hdescent : ((RingHom.ker presentation).comap
        (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
          ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)).comp (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
        = (RingHom.ker presentation).map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L))) :
    L ⊗[A₀] restriction.range ≃ₐ[L] L ⊗[A] T :=
  (Algebra.TensorProduct.congr (AlgEquiv.refl (R := L))
      (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective restriction.rangeRestrict_surjective).symm).trans
    ((Algebra.TensorProduct.congr (AlgEquiv.refl (R := L))
      (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq A₀
        ((AlgHom.ker_rangeRestrict restriction).trans
          (MvPolynomial.ker_restriction_eq_comap_ker presentation restriction
            hrestriction)))).trans
      ((MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv _ hdescent).trans
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.congr (AlgEquiv.refl (R := L))
          (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hsurjective))))

/-- `MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv` is the inclusion of the descended subalgebra on the
right-hand factor: it sends `c ⊗ x` to `c ⊗ x`. -/
public theorem MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv_tmul
    {A₀ A T L : Type*} [CommRing A₀] [CommRing A] [CommRing T] [CommRing L]
    [Algebra A₀ A] [Algebra A T] [Algebra A₀ T] [IsScalarTower A₀ A T]
    [Algebra A L] [Algebra A₀ L] [IsScalarTower A₀ A L]
    {σ : Type*} (presentation : MvPolynomial σ A →ₐ[A] T)
    (hsurjective : Function.Surjective presentation)
    (restriction : MvPolynomial σ A₀ →ₐ[A₀] T)
    (hrestriction : ∀ f, restriction f = presentation (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A) f))
    (hdescent : ((RingHom.ker presentation).comap
        (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A))).map
          ((MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)).comp (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A₀ A)))
        = (RingHom.ker presentation).map (MvPolynomial.map (algebraMap A L)))
    (c : L) (x : restriction.range) :
    MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv presentation hsurjective restriction hrestriction hdescent
        (c ⊗ₜ[A₀] x) = c ⊗ₜ[A] (x : T) := by
  obtain ⟨f, rfl⟩ := restriction.rangeRestrict_surjective x
  simp only [MvPolynomial.tensorRangeAlgEquiv, AlgEquiv.trans_apply,
    Algebra.TensorProduct.congr_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul, AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom]
  rw [Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective_symm_apply]
  simp only [Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq_mk]
  rw [MvPolynomial.tensorQuotientComapAlgEquiv_tmul_mk]
  simp only [Algebra.TensorProduct.map_tmul,
    AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom, Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective_mk]
  rw [← hrestriction]
  rfl

/-!
### Residue field extensions
-/

/-- The residue field extension `κ(𝔭) → κ(𝔭')` induced by a ring map `R → R'` at a prime `𝔭'` of
`R'` and the prime `𝔭` of `R` it lies over. -/
public noncomputable abbrev Ideal.residueFieldAlgebra {R R' : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing R']
    [Algebra R R'] (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] (p' : Ideal R') [p'.IsPrime] [p'.LiesOver p] :
    Algebra p.ResidueField p'.ResidueField :=
  (Ideal.ResidueField.map p p' (algebraMap R R') (Ideal.over_def p' p)).toAlgebra

attribute [local instance] Ideal.residueFieldAlgebra

/-- The residue field extension `κ(𝔭) → κ(𝔭')` is a map of `R`-algebras. -/
public theorem Ideal.isScalarTower_residueField {R R' : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing R']
    [Algebra R R'] (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] (p' : Ideal R') [p'.IsPrime] [p'.LiesOver p] :
    IsScalarTower R p.ResidueField p'.ResidueField :=
  .of_algebraMap_eq fun x => by
    simp [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R R' p'.ResidueField]

/-- A residue field extension is injective. -/
public theorem Ideal.residueFieldMap_injective {R R' : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing R']
    [Algebra R R'] (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] (p' : Ideal R') [p'.IsPrime] [p'.LiesOver p] :
    Function.Injective (Ideal.ResidueField.map p p' (algebraMap R R') (Ideal.over_def p' p)) :=
  RingHom.injective _

/-!
### Descent along a faithfully flat map
-/

/-- Units descend along a faithfully flat algebra map. -/
public theorem IsUnit.of_faithfullyFlat {S T : Type*} [CommRing S] [CommRing T] [Algebra S T]
    [Module.FaithfullyFlat S T] (x : S) (h : IsUnit (algebraMap S T x)) : IsUnit x :=
  (isUnit_map_iff (algebraMap S T) x).mp h

/-- Non-units ascend along any algebra map: if `algebraMap S T x` is not a unit then neither
is `x`. -/
public theorem not_isUnit_of_faithfullyFlat {S T : Type*} [CommRing S] [CommRing T] [Algebra S T]
    (x : S) (h : ¬ IsUnit (algebraMap S T x)) : ¬ IsUnit x :=
  fun hx => h (hx.map (algebraMap S T))

/-- Avoidance of the minimal primes descends along a faithfully flat algebra map. -/
public theorem Ideal.notMem_minimalPrimes_of_faithfullyFlat {S T : Type*} [CommRing S]
    [CommRing T] [Algebra S T] [Module.FaithfullyFlat S T] (x : S)
    (h : ∀ Q ∈ minimalPrimes T, algebraMap S T x ∉ Q) :
    ∀ q ∈ minimalPrimes S, x ∉ q := by
  have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap S T) := FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective S T
  intro q hq hxq
  have hq' : q ∈ ((⊥ : Ideal T).comap (algebraMap S T)).minimalPrimes := by
    rwa [Ideal.comap_bot_of_injective _ hinj]
  obtain ⟨Q, hQ, hQq⟩ := Ideal.exists_minimalPrimes_comap_eq (algebraMap S T) q hq'
  rw [← hQq] at hxq
  exact h Q hQ hxq

/-- Faithful flatness ascends along a base change: in a pushout square `T = K ⊗[k] S`, if `K` is
faithfully flat over `k` then `T` is faithfully flat over `S`. -/
@[ega "0 6.6.3" "special case", ega "IV 2.2.11" "(i), special case"]
public theorem Module.FaithfullyFlat.of_isPushout {k K S T : Type*} [CommRing k] [CommRing K]
    [CommRing S] [CommRing T] [Algebra k K] [Algebra k S] [Algebra k T] [Algebra K T]
    [Algebra S T] [IsScalarTower k K T] [IsScalarTower k S T] [Algebra.IsPushout k K S T]
    [Module.FaithfullyFlat k K] : Module.FaithfullyFlat S T :=
  have : Algebra.IsPushout k S K T := Algebra.IsPushout.symm ‹_›
  have : Module.FaithfullyFlat S (S ⊗[k] K) := inferInstance
  Module.FaithfullyFlat.of_linearEquiv S (S ⊗[k] K)
    (Algebra.IsPushout.equiv k S K T).symm.toLinearEquiv

/-- Finite type ascends along a base change: in a pushout square `T = K ⊗[k] S`, if `S` is of
finite type over `k` then `T` is of finite type over `K`. -/
public theorem Algebra.FiniteType.of_isPushout {k K S T : Type*} [CommRing k] [CommRing K]
    [CommRing S] [CommRing T] [Algebra k K] [Algebra k S] [Algebra k T] [Algebra K T]
    [Algebra S T] [IsScalarTower k K T] [IsScalarTower k S T] [Algebra.IsPushout k K S T]
    [Algebra.FiniteType k S] : Algebra.FiniteType K T :=
  Algebra.FiniteType.equiv inferInstance (Algebra.IsPushout.equiv k K S T)

end
